        "label": "dg_spec",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "type",
            "name": "dg_spec"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "An analysis is a record with one transfer per edge action plus the call and return operations, matching Goblint's method-per-construct shape. Spec's startstate, exitstate and morphstate have no counterpart."
    },
    {
      "status": "simplified",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "D / G lattices",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/framework/analyses.ml#L170-L173",
        "file": "src/framework/analyses.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "'dl / 'dg carriers",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "type",
            "name": "dg_spec"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "The local/global split exists, but the shipped domains keep their whole state local."
    },
    {
      "status": "simplified",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "TD3 solver",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/solver/td3.ml#L1-L50",
        "file": "src/solver/td3.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "Top-down solver with side effects",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "locale",
            "name": "TD_side_upd_rule"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "Vendored from td-verification with a partial-correctness proof; it has neither Goblint's sidel nor its demandl."
    },
    {
      "status": "simplified",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "sidel into a function entry",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/framework/constraints.ml#L242-L245",
        "file": "src/framework/constraints.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "Side effect into an entry proxy",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "type",
            "name": "routed_gk"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "A callee entry is published to a global proxy key and read back by the entry's local unknown, so it widens one hop later; no equivalence to Goblint's fixpoint is claimed."
    },
    {
      "status": "modeled",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "enter returning alternatives",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/framework/analyses.ml#L233-L237",
        "file": "src/framework/analyses.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "dgs_enter",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "const",
            "name": "dgs_enter"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "A list of alternatives, each a pair of caller continuation and callee entry state; the call-site equation routes each alternative and joins their contributions."
    },
    {
      "status": "modeled",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "context from the callee state",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/framework/analyses.ml#L196-L197",
        "file": "src/framework/analyses.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "Context selector on the entered state",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "locale",
            "name": "routed_context_base_hetero"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "The context is chosen from the state after enter, as in Goblint, though the selector does not see which callee it is choosing for."
    },
    {
      "status": "simplified",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "combine_env / combine_assign",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/framework/analyses.ml#L239-L251",
        "file": "src/framework/analyses.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "dgs_combine_env / dgs_combine_assign",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "const",
            "name": "dgs_combine_env"
          },
          {
            "kind": "const",
            "name": "dgs_combine_assign"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "Both hooks exist: the specifications the analyses execute split the environment merge from the return write, as Goblint does; only the proof-side whole-state specifications leave the environment merge the identity."
    },
    {
      "status": "simplified",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "Widening and narrowing",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/solver/td3.ml#L381-L394",
        "file": "src/solver/td3.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "Four global update rules",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "type",
            "name": "globals_rule"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "Local unknowns are warrowed at widening points under every rule; the merge rule for side-effected globals is chosen once per run, not per unknown."
    },
    {
      "status": "simplified",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "Context-sensitivity options",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/analyses/callstring.ml#L19-L55",
        "file": "src/analyses/callstring.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "None, entry state, call strings",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "type",
            "name": "context_mode"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "Bounded call strings give a finite context space over a compiled program; nothing certifies that entry-state contexts stay finite, and lifters such as context gas are absent."
    },
    {
      "status": "simplified",
      "goblint": {
        "name": "IntDomTuple",
        "url": "https://github.com/goblint/analyzer/blob/5320a6b741e50dc049f7a1b85e1709e9565cc54a/src/cdomain/value/cdomains/int/intDomTuple.ml#L14-L27",
        "file": "src/cdomain/value/cdomains/int/intDomTuple.ml"
      },
      "voblint": {
        "label": "Int product: sign × interval × parity × congruence",
        "refs": [
          {
            "kind": "type",
            "name": "int_dom"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "Goblint combines six optional integer domains; only interval and congruence have counterparts here, and sign and parity have none upstream. A DefExc-style exclusion component cannot form the required lattice over unbounded integers; that argument is recorded in the alignment register, not machine-checked."
    },
